diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..f6df0bd 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,56 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+Requires Node.js 24 or newer. Account creation and sign-in support either a
+password or a discoverable WebAuthn passkey. After signing in, open **Account &
+security** in the header to add, rename, or remove passkeys and verify your identity.
+Sensitive changes require authentication within the last five minutes. Users with
+no password must keep at least one passkey; adding a backup is recommended.
+
+Authentication now uses the application's own server, rather than the external
+demo login/register service. Accounts previously created in that service are not
+migrated and must be registered locally. Passwords are salted and hashed with
+scrypt; only public keys and credential metadata are stored for passkeys.
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm dev
+# Open http://localhost:4321/devtools-times/
+```
+
+For a production build:
+
+```sh
+pnpm build
+AUTH_ORIGIN=https://your-domain.example AUTH_DB_PATH=/persistent-data/auth.sqlite pnpm start
+```
+
+- `AUTH_ORIGIN`: public origin, including the port when needed, without a path.
+  Set this explicitly behind a proxy. Defaults to the request origin for local
+  development. The origin's hostname is the WebAuthn relying party ID.
+- `AUTH_DB_PATH`: SQLite database location; defaults to `.data/auth.sqlite`.
+  Use a persistent, private, writable volume and back it up. This SQLite setup
+  supports a single application instance; multiple replicas need shared storage
+  and an appropriate database implementation.
+- Passkeys require HTTPS, except on localhost. Credentials belong to the hostname
+  where they were registered; changing hosts requires new passkeys.
+- Challenges expire after five minutes and are consumed once. Sessions are stored
+  server-side, rotate on authentication, and expire after seven days. Cookies are
+  HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, and Secure over HTTPS. POST endpoints enforce the origin
+  and apply per-address request limits.
+
+Automated verification (no browser required):
+
+```sh
+pnpm test # builds the app and runs the tests
+pnpm check
+```
+
+The tests run the built server against a temporary SQLite database and use signed
+WebAuthn registration/authentication fixtures. `pnpm check` also reports existing
+unrelated type errors in the news/image/menu components.
+Implementation follows the [SimpleWebAuthn server](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/packages/server)
+and [passkey guidance](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/advanced/passkeys/).
